Package: thirdreality-matter2mqtt
Version: 1.4.0-tr.3
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Depends: thirdreality-python3
Maintainer: guoping.liu <guoping.liu@3reality.com>
Description: Matter-to-MQTT gateway (matter.js server fork + native MQTT bridge), no Home Assistant.
 Exposes Matter devices, their state, control, commissioning and firmware updates over MQTT
 in a zigbee2mqtt-style topic layout, including Home Assistant MQTT discovery. Based on the
 ThirdReality matterjs-server fork (matter-server 1.4.0 / matter.js 0.17.9), whose
 packages/mqtt-bridge is enabled with --mqtt-url; the earlier "official npm package plus
 @matter/mqtt patches" approach is retired. BLE commissioning uses a standalone
 matter-ble-proxy venv (bleak/BlueZ, Python 3.14 from thirdreality-python3), coexisting
 with bluetoothd. Node.js is taken from the system runtime (>=22.13). Connects to the
 system mosquitto (provided by zigbee2mqtt / the OS); does not install or configure it.
